Manual review corrections, all local LaTeX/typographic defects rather than
mathematical errors:

1. Twenty-eight "from ... to ..." interval descriptions across this file
   fused the English words "from"/"to" into the surrounding math span via
   \,\text{from}\,/\,\text{to}\,, gluing separate equations to plain-prose
   connectives inside math mode (e.g. "$y=5x\,\text{from}\,x=0\,\text{to}\,
   x=2$"). Several sibling exercises in the very same lists already use the
   file's own correctly split convention ("$y=\sqrt{x}$ from $x=2$ to
   $x=6$"), and this matches the corpus-wide convention used throughout
   other reviewed files (e.g. vol3-3-3-arc-length-and-curvature.tex: "from
   $x=0$ to $x=5$"). Split every fused instance into separate math spans
   with plain "from"/"to" prose between them, matching the file's own
   majority convention.

2. Four exercises carry redundant outer braces around an already-
   parenthesized base before a fractional exponent, {(x^{2}+2)}^{3/2},
   {(x^{2}-2)}^{3/2}, {(9x^{2}+6)}^{3/2}, and {(y^{2}+1)}^{3/2} (matching a
   previously found defect of the same shape in
   vol2-2-3-volumes-of-revolution-cylindrical-shells.tex). Removed the
   redundant braces in all four: (x^{2}+2)^{3/2}, (x^{2}-2)^{3/2},
   (9x^{2}+6)^{3/2}, (y^{2}+1)^{3/2}.

3. Three coordinate pairs carry an erratic manual \, before the second
   coordinate, $(1,\,1)$ (twice) and $(2,\,2)$, while every other
   coordinate pair in this file (fourteen occurrences) uses a plain comma
   with no extra spacing, e.g. $(1,1)$, $(0,0)$, $(8,4)$. Removed the
   erratic \, in all three to match the file's own overwhelming
   convention: $(1,1)$, $(1,1)$, $(2,2)$.

No mathematical content, numbering, or exercise substance was altered.

